                {
                    "file": "utility.cpp",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "This should probably be ENTITY_MGR_SERVICE.  This is a D-Bus service name, not an interface name.\n\nI realize the constant used for the Inventory Manager service is called INVENTORY_IFACE.  That is a confusing special case, because it is both a service name and a D-Bus interface.  But I don't think we should copy that naming convention.\n\nAlso, it would be more helpful if this were moved to types.hpp.  That is included by this file, and it has a lot of the common service, interface, and property names.  That would make the constant reusable by other code that deals with EntityManager.\n\nThe Slot constants can stay here, as that is more internal detail and could change in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "utility.cpp",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
